outputs.L1:
The present invention relates to a method for producing and/or capturing neutrons, comprising the following steps:

a) exposing nuclei selected from protons, deuterons, and/or tritons to an electric field so as to extract said nuclei and direct the extracted nuclei toward a target (20) containing free electrons;

b) optionally, subjecting said nuclei to a spatial and/or temporal gradient of a first magnetic field in order to impart a predefined orientation to the nuclear magnetic moments;

c) either subjecting the target to a second magnetic field in order to impart a predefined orientation to the magnetic moments of the target's free electrons;

d) or employing an electron-donor superparamagnetic material, such that the electrons within the free layers of said material are oriented along preferred directions determined by the orientation of the resulting magnetic moment of the superparamagnetic material;

e) optionally, when a superparamagnetic material is employed, refraining from exposing the proton beam and/or the target to external magnetic fields.

A heating device and/or a device for generating magnetic fields may be required to activate the superparamagnetic properties of the material.

