Here is a paraphrased version of the text:

This invention presents a technique for generating and/or trapping neutrons, comprising the following stages:

a) Nuclear particles—specifically protons, deuterons, and/or tritons—are subjected to an electric field, which pulls these particles free and channels them toward a target (20) that contains free electrons;

b) Optionally, these nuclear particles may be passed through a spatial and/or temporal gradient within an initial magnetic field, thereby aligning the nuclei's magnetic moments in a specific direction;

c) Alternatively, the target itself can be placed within a second magnetic field, which aligns the magnetic moments of its free electrons in a predetermined direction;

d) As another option, an electron-donating superparamagnetic material may be employed, causing electrons within its free layers to align along preferential directions determined by the overall magnetic moment orientation of the superparamagnetic substance;

e) When a superparamagnetic material is utilized, the proton beam and/or target need not be subjected to any external magnetic fields, as an optional variation.

To trigger the superparamagnetic behavior of the material, a heating apparatus and/or a magnetic field generation device may be necessary.
